01:11:17.216 --> 01:11:19.326
like a family pet has just died.

01:11:19.326 --> 01:11:20.777
- Yeah, yeah.
- You know?

01:11:20.777 --> 01:11:22.955
It's like, it's something
that, it really is,

01:11:22.955 --> 01:11:24.013
it's like, it's honestly,
it's that same emotion.

01:11:24.013 --> 01:11:25.603
- Honestly, I started fucking bawling man

01:11:25.603 --> 01:11:29.925
'cause like, here's the thing,
I wasn't even hyped for 4.0.

01:11:29.925 --> 01:11:32.526
Right 'cause like nine years
had passed since the fast,

01:11:32.526 --> 01:11:34.075
since the last week and I'm just like,

01:11:34.075 --> 01:11:37.766
whatever, it's out, I'll
watch it out of obligation.

01:11:37.766 --> 01:11:40.726
I love Eva but I don't,
I could go my entire life

01:11:40.726 --> 01:11:42.816
without watching another Evangelion movie

01:11:42.816 --> 01:11:44.656
and I would have been
completely satisfied.

01:11:44.656 --> 01:11:47.466
So I watched it literally out
of obligation and then like,

01:11:47.466 --> 01:11:50.443
I think the last half hour
hit and I'm just like,

01:11:50.443 --> 01:11:52.456
"Oh my God, what is this
I'm feeling right now?

01:11:52.456 --> 01:11:56.646
Is this a feeling of
closure, am I closing a page

01:11:56.646 --> 01:11:58.633
in my life right now?" I'm just like,

01:11:58.633 --> 01:12:00.166
"What is this feeling?"
- Yeah.

01:12:00.166 --> 01:12:03.336
- And then the end credits,
felt like the end credits

01:12:03.336 --> 01:12:06.816
started rolling and I just,
process is the right word

01:12:06.816 --> 01:12:09.899
because there are so many
emotions coming up at once

01:12:09.899 --> 01:12:12.733
that I just, I didn't know
how to process them all

01:12:12.733 --> 01:12:15.826
and you just felt empty
and you just felt like,

01:12:15.826 --> 01:12:20.434
I felt like a fucking void
in my life and I'm just like,

01:12:20.434 --> 01:12:23.415
there's nothing that's going
to fill this hole up anymore.

01:12:23.415 --> 01:12:24.963
That's why I need to talk about it.

01:12:24.963 --> 01:12:26.709
That's why I'm so desperate to, because-

01:12:26.709 --> 01:12:29.956
- Because I remember as well,
like when the first posters

01:12:29.956 --> 01:12:33.006
for 4.0 released in
Japan, the tagline for it

01:12:33.006 --> 01:12:36.006
was (speaking Japanese) which
means goodbye Evangelion

01:12:36.006 --> 01:12:38.404
and I was like, okay, that's
kind of a cool, very, you know-

01:12:38.404 --> 01:12:42.666
like very like artistic,
like kind of tagline.

01:12:42.666 --> 01:12:44.196
I didn't think anything of it, right?

01:12:44.196 --> 01:12:46.116
But then when they said
that line in the movie

01:12:46.116 --> 01:12:48.653
at a particular scene, I was like,

01:12:48.653 --> 01:12:50.266
"No,

01:12:50.266 --> 01:12:53.401
don't do this to me man, don't leave me!"

01:12:53.401 --> 01:12:56.602
- "I'm sorry, I should
have treated you better"

01:12:56.602 --> 01:12:57.737
- "I should have treated you better.

01:12:57.737 --> 01:12:59.176
I should have treated
you more, more, right.

01:12:59.176 --> 01:13:00.756
Don't leave me, not now"

01:13:00.756 --> 01:13:02.336
and like that was the moment

01:13:02.336 --> 01:13:03.980
where I was like, oh, okay like this,

01:13:03.980 --> 01:13:06.926
that point I think really solidified to me

01:13:06.926 --> 01:13:08.836
how important this series was to me.

01:13:08.836 --> 01:13:11.186
- I'd forgotten it was until that moment

01:13:11.186 --> 01:13:12.766
and like, I've been doing ever since,

01:13:12.766 --> 01:13:14.658
I've ever since that movie I could,

01:13:14.658 --> 01:13:16.326
I've not been able to watch anything else.

01:13:16.326 --> 01:13:18.306
I've not been able to play any games.

01:13:18.306 --> 01:13:19.520
I just feel like the emptiness.

01:13:19.520 --> 01:13:22.846
- You literally can't
consume any other media

01:13:22.846 --> 01:13:24.155
for at least a week.
- Yeah.

01:13:24.155 --> 01:13:25.353
'Cause like I tried to and I'm just like,

01:13:25.353 --> 01:13:28.146
"This ain't Eva, what's the point?"

01:13:28.146 --> 01:13:30.626
- That's why I'm really
scared to rewatch it.

01:13:30.626 --> 01:13:32.636
- Yeah.
- I tried playing League.

01:13:32.636 --> 01:13:33.927
Lost, I'm just like, "Don't care"

01:13:33.927 --> 01:13:35.596
- Is that how it should all be ending?

01:13:35.596 --> 01:13:39.107
- I was just like, nothing's
going to fill this void.

01:13:39.107 --> 01:13:39.940
- It's like that moment after you cum.

01:13:39.940 --> 01:13:43.519
You just don't feel anything,
you just sit there like,

01:13:43.519 --> 01:13:45.159
no emotion.
- I think I've just

01:13:45.159 --> 01:13:49.536
reached Zen, like I feel like
I've reached enlightenment.

01:13:49.536 --> 01:13:51.636
Like fuck being a monk, man, like is this

01:13:51.636 --> 01:13:54.526
what it feels like, you
just like an open book

01:13:54.526 --> 01:13:56.143
and you just like, I finally-
- Who would have thought

01:13:56.143 --> 01:13:59.546
you could become a monk
with a 6.99 membership.

01:13:59.546 --> 01:14:03.496
- I'm finally at peace with
my life and now I just want

01:14:03.496 --> 01:14:06.231
to get the hell this on, I
just want to move on now.

01:14:06.231 --> 01:14:09.186
- So for anyone watching
this who's never seen Eva,

01:14:09.186 --> 01:14:12.206
we're not coming onto here
saying that we recommend you

01:14:12.206 --> 01:14:14.262
to watch Eva, it's hard to recommend-

01:14:14.262 --> 01:14:16.141
- It's hard to recommend
now because you're not

01:14:16.141 --> 01:14:16.974
going to have the same experience

01:14:16.974 --> 01:14:18.136
that we had where you just like,

01:14:18.136 --> 01:14:20.809
where you grew up with this,
so, and you know, like I said,

01:14:20.809 --> 01:14:23.796
if you're someone who's going
in a tough time in your life,

01:14:23.796 --> 01:14:26.986
then I honestly recommend
you experience it

01:14:26.986 --> 01:14:28.801
because maybe it will teach
you something about yourself.

01:14:28.801 --> 01:14:29.821
- I was gonna say, I was like,

01:14:29.821 --> 01:14:33.546
you know, if you haven't had any struggles

01:14:33.546 --> 01:14:34.716
with mental health, is it hard

01:14:34.716 --> 01:14:36.226
to appreciate stuff like that?

01:14:36.226 --> 01:14:37.226
- I think so.
- I think so.

01:14:37.226 --> 01:14:39.626
- Because like after I watched Eva,

01:14:39.626 --> 01:14:41.376
I've like, I've just been binge-watching

01:14:41.376 --> 01:14:43.829
so many like Eva analysis videos but like-

01:14:44.799 --> 01:14:46.066
- I'm the same.
- Which is like,

01:14:46.066 --> 01:14:47.776
I guess like my way of coping.

01:14:47.776 --> 01:14:50.766
- I think Ken and I had
about a six hour conversation

01:14:50.766 --> 01:14:53.766
and Hezekiah about just
the movie we just watched,

01:14:53.766 --> 01:14:54.886
the entire time.

01:14:54.886 --> 01:14:57.246
- Yeah and I think the video

01:14:57.246 --> 01:15:02.246
that I like related to the
most in terms of what I felt

01:15:02.256 --> 01:15:03.856
when I watched the first time was-

01:15:03.856 --> 01:15:07.163
- Was Eva abridged.
- No no, no, no.

01:15:07.163 --> 01:15:08.976
Scamboni Reviews

01:15:08.976 --> 01:15:11.256
did a video called "You
Don't Understand Eva"

01:15:11.256 --> 01:15:12.919
right?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:15:12.919 --> 01:15:14.684
- In like sarcastic text, you know,

01:15:14.684 --> 01:15:19.006
where he basically broke
down why Eva is like,

01:15:19.006 --> 01:15:21.745
basically a really badly told plot.

01:15:21.745 --> 01:15:26.056
Like he basically broke it down

01:15:26.056 --> 01:15:29.346
in a way where I
completely agreed with him.

01:15:29.346 --> 01:15:30.806
I would've completely agreed with them.

01:15:30.806 --> 01:15:33.616
'Cause that was basically
what I was trying to say

01:15:33.616 --> 01:15:37.966
when I had watched first time
because I just didn't resonate

01:15:37.966 --> 01:15:39.789
or relate to anything
that was trying to say.

01:15:39.789 --> 01:15:42.916
- No, me neither, you know,
I didn't really feel sorry

01:15:42.916 --> 01:15:45.325
for Shinji at all, I felt
like I was supposed to.

01:15:45.325 --> 01:15:48.155
- That's the thing,
the emotions were there

01:15:48.155 --> 01:15:49.646
but the execution was not there.

01:15:49.646 --> 01:15:52.046
- I mean, like, I don't think
like you were even supposed

01:15:52.046 --> 01:15:55.066
to feel sorry for him,
right because yeah, exactly.

01:15:55.066 --> 01:15:57.056
like either you do feel sorry for him

01:15:57.056 --> 01:15:59.096
or you don't, like a
lot of people would do

01:15:59.096 --> 01:16:02.056
because a lot of people relate
to that kind of mental space.

01:16:02.056 --> 01:16:03.156
Right that they can resonate with that

01:16:03.156 --> 01:16:06.446
but like the series doesn't
explicitly tell you,

01:16:06.446 --> 01:16:08.704
you should feel sorry for this
person, this person is this,

01:16:08.704 --> 01:16:11.435
it's just, that's kind of like,

01:16:11.435 --> 01:16:15.356
that's kind of like the
thing that maybe like not,

01:16:15.356 --> 01:16:18.536
not everyone will enjoy Eva,
not everyone should enjoy it.

01:16:18.536 --> 01:16:20.636
I mean, I wouldn't recommend it to someone

01:16:20.636 --> 01:16:22.866
in a very healthy mental
state because one,

01:16:22.866 --> 01:16:24.136
you probably wouldn't get it and two,

01:16:24.136 --> 01:16:26.376
I wouldn't wish for you to
be in a bad mental state

01:16:26.376 --> 01:16:28.116
to begin with to get it, right, yeah.

01:16:28.116 --> 01:16:31.166
- I mean, you know,
BoJack, I thought was great

01:16:31.166 --> 01:16:33.066
'cause I wasn't depressed watching it

01:16:33.066 --> 01:16:34.925
but I certainly was after.
- Well, yeah,

01:16:34.925 --> 01:16:37.926
I mean like things like
BoJack and like, you know,

01:16:37.926 --> 01:16:40.063
we related Eva to BoJack
but I think like something

01:16:40.063 --> 01:16:41.646
like Oyasumi PunPun. is probably closer

01:16:41.646 --> 01:16:43.316
in terms of like actually, you know,

01:16:43.316 --> 01:16:47.246
presenting a very sad story
in a way that can get anyone

01:16:47.246 --> 01:16:50.933
of any mental state invested
in the story of BoJack, right?

01:16:50.933 --> 01:16:53.866
Like, you know, BoJack
in that case was told

01:16:53.866 --> 01:16:55.166
in a very like straightforward,

01:16:55.166 --> 01:16:56.743
like here's the thing that's fucked up.

01:16:56.743 --> 01:16:58.636
You know, this is why
you should feel sorry

01:16:58.636 --> 01:17:00.429
and for most people, they felt sorry.

01:17:00.429 --> 01:17:01.348
- [Connor] It was very easily presented.

01:17:01.348 --> 01:17:02.181
- It was, yeah, easily presented but like,

01:17:02.181 --> 01:17:05.786
I feel Eva in that
sense is almost so vague

01:17:05.786 --> 01:17:08.616
with what they want the viewer to feel.

01:17:08.616 --> 01:17:09.516
- Yeah.
- To the point

01:17:09.516 --> 01:17:11.376
where it's like, here are the emotions

01:17:11.376 --> 01:17:13.586
that you should be feeling but
we're not going to tell you

01:17:13.586 --> 01:17:15.116
to feel those emotions specifically.

01:17:15.116 --> 01:17:16.906
That's up to you to decide.
- Yeah.

01:17:16.906 --> 01:17:18.836
- Kind of thing.
- Like, I don't trust anyone

01:17:18.836 --> 01:17:23.501
who says they understand Eva,
like you can spend all like-

01:17:23.501 --> 01:17:25.976
- It just sounds like you
can have an interpretation

01:17:25.976 --> 01:17:26.809
of Eva.
- You can

01:17:26.809 --> 01:17:28.368
have an interpretation of Eva.
- Oh, there's many,

01:17:28.368 --> 01:17:29.201
many interpretations.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:17:29.201 --> 01:17:31.726
- But to claim to understand
Eva I feel like is just,

01:17:31.726 --> 01:17:33.283
I don't, I honestly
don't think it's possible

01:17:33.283 --> 01:17:36.059
and I'm sure there are some
Eva fans that are out there

01:17:36.059 --> 01:17:38.286
that are just like, I
can't believe he said that.

01:17:38.286 --> 01:17:39.160
- Um, actually.
(laughter)

01:17:39.160 --> 01:17:42.586
- But like I've spent
so many fucking hours

01:17:42.586 --> 01:17:44.216
watching different people analyze it,

01:17:44.216 --> 01:17:46.196
different people's
interpretation but like,

01:17:46.196 --> 01:17:48.626
there are so many different
interpretations of the series

01:17:48.626 --> 01:17:52.636
to begin with that I just
think that's the thing, right?

01:17:52.636 --> 01:17:55.256
There's a reason why we
are still discussing it

01:17:55.256 --> 01:17:56.506
to this day 26 years later.
- Yeah.

01:17:56.506 --> 01:17:58.646
- And I think it'll always be discussed.

01:17:58.646 --> 01:18:00.596
- I remember, it was
a couple of years ago,

01:18:00.596 --> 01:18:03.446
I think like when we
were still in the rush

01:18:03.446 --> 01:18:05.186
of all these people, you know,

01:18:05.186 --> 01:18:07.786
just analyzing every
single piece of imagery

01:18:07.786 --> 01:18:10.526
from the TV series, right and
one that got discussed a lot

01:18:10.526 --> 01:18:13.346
was when the angels explode,
they create an explosion

01:18:13.346 --> 01:18:15.056
that looks like a cross.
- Yeah.

01:18:15.056 --> 01:18:17.356
- And there was, I watched
so many analysis videos

01:18:17.356 --> 01:18:19.806
being like, this is why
Anno chose the cross

01:18:19.806 --> 01:18:22.036
and why it's super symbolic
and blah, blah, blah

01:18:22.036 --> 01:18:23.246
and then a couple of years later,

01:18:23.246 --> 01:18:24.416
they came out with an interview with Anno

01:18:24.416 --> 01:18:27.406
and they were asking,
"So is there any reason

01:18:27.406 --> 01:18:29.716
why when the angels explodes,
it turns into a cross?"

01:18:29.716 --> 01:18:31.119
And he literally just said,

01:18:31.119 --> 01:18:32.264
"I just think it looks cool"

01:18:32.264 --> 01:18:33.097
(laughter)

01:18:33.097 --> 01:18:36.486
It doesn't mean anything
and all the anime YouTubers

01:18:36.486 --> 01:18:39.492
were like, "We spent all
this time analyzing something

01:18:39.492 --> 01:18:43.261
that you just put in
because it looks cool?"

01:18:43.261 --> 01:18:48.261
And I feel like that alone
to me really showed the fact

01:18:48.486 --> 01:18:50.876
that Anno doesn't think this shit is deep.

01:18:50.876 --> 01:18:52.026
He just put it in because it's cool.

01:18:52.026 --> 01:18:54.746
- Also, if you're saying that
you didn't have time or money

01:18:54.746 --> 01:18:56.306
to make a proper ending-
- Yeah.

01:18:56.306 --> 01:18:57.446
- What's the odds that he had the time

01:18:57.446 --> 01:18:59.266
to be able to be like, no,
no, no change the explosion

01:18:59.266 --> 01:19:00.196
to a cross.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:19:00.196 --> 01:19:02.226
Like this is why you should do this

01:19:02.226 --> 01:19:03.346
because it's symbolic to the story.

01:19:03.346 --> 01:19:05.549
No, because it's just a love letter

01:19:06.597 --> 01:19:07.430
to all the shit Ano likes, he's like,

01:19:07.430 --> 01:19:09.806
I think the cross looks
cool, let's add that shit in.

01:19:09.806 --> 01:19:11.039
- Yeah, I mean, at the same time,

01:19:11.039 --> 01:19:13.376
I would say that maybe he
didn't make a conscious choice.

01:19:13.376 --> 01:19:15.166
He put stuff in just
because it felt right.

01:19:15.166 --> 01:19:17.246
It looked right and it
created a certain tone,

01:19:17.246 --> 01:19:18.636
a certain mood, whatever.
- Especially in 4.0.

01:19:18.636 --> 01:19:21.444
- And you can analyze that
but to say that everything

01:19:21.444 --> 01:19:24.245
had a purpose and everything
was put there for a reason,

01:19:24.245 --> 01:19:26.353
I think, no, no, not everything in Eva,

01:19:26.353 --> 01:19:28.756
I don't think Anno knew everything

01:19:28.756 --> 01:19:29.699
that he knew what he wanted to say in Eva.

01:19:29.699 --> 01:19:31.696
- I think especially in 4.0 as well,

01:19:31.696 --> 01:19:33.107
there was so much shit in there, I'm like,

01:19:33.107 --> 01:19:37.556
that doesn't make any
sense, why is that there?

01:19:37.556 --> 01:19:39.066
Oh, fuck it, you know what is on there?

01:19:39.066 --> 01:19:40.236
Just let him do what he wants to do.

01:19:40.236 --> 01:19:41.069
Yeah.
- Well, I guess

01:19:41.069 --> 01:19:43.347
like moving on from
like Eva as a franchise,

01:19:43.347 --> 01:19:46.238
we can like tag you back in now, Connor.

01:19:46.238 --> 01:19:47.767
We can tag you back in.

01:19:47.767 --> 01:19:48.756
(Joey laughs)

01:19:48.756 --> 01:19:50.316
Like, has it been any other

01:19:50.316 --> 01:19:53.056
like points or like series or franchise

01:19:53.056 --> 01:19:54.666
where you've kind of like grown up with

01:19:54.666 --> 01:19:57.326
that franchise and you've had like,

01:19:57.326 --> 01:19:59.756
you've seen the franchise come
back years and years later

01:19:59.756 --> 01:20:02.846
